                Blocks(Paragraph(Text("The exact compiled declaration retains an arbitrary commutative ring R, d, the full d by d+1 matrix M, vector x, original kernel equation hx, and coordinate i. For a d by d+1 matrix over any commutative ring and a vector in its kernel, the determinant of the matrix augmented by a first row of ones times coordinate i equals the sum of the vector coordinates times signed cofactor i. The sign is (-1) to the column index and the minor deletes that column by succAbove. This is the classical adjugate/cofactor expansion identity used by the integer-kernel results. Over the reals, a strictly positive kernel vector and one nonzero cofactor force a nonzero augmented determinant and positive proportionality after choosing an orientation. The nonnegative-kernel cofactor completeness theorem consumes this identity; selected-row kernel membership alone does not establish the original row equations."))),
